airplay: hand the speaker's play/pause to listeners instead of the player

A HomePod's touch surface sends play, pause, next and previous over
the AirPlay event channel as sendMediaRemoteCommand, and owntone
applied them to its player. With a pipe as the source that is
destructive: pause closes and reopens the pipe, the process writing
it (librespot) gets EPIPE and exits, and play then restarts the item
at position 0. Next and previous mean nothing inside a pipe.

Pause and play become listener events, LISTENER_REMOTE_PAUSE and
LISTENER_REMOTE_PLAY, which the websocket carries as "remote_pause"
and "remote_play" to any client that subscribed to them, so the
client driving this server decides what a speaker's pause should do.
Next and previous are dropped at INFO.

--- a/src/listener.h
+++ b/src/listener.h
@@ -28,6 +28,9 @@
   LISTENER_LASTFM = (1 << 10),
   /* Song rating changes */
   LISTENER_RATING = (1 << 11),
+  /* A speaker asked, over its own controls, for playback to pause or play */
+  LISTENER_REMOTE_PAUSE = (1 << 12),
+  LISTENER_REMOTE_PLAY = (1 << 13),
 };
 
 typedef void (*notify)(short event_mask, void *ctx);
